A **transformer** raises or lowers an alternating voltage by a chosen factor without changing its frequency.
We first describe this process with an ideal, low-loss approximation;
a real device still consumes some of the input power.

This lesson defines the **transformation coefficient** $K$ as primary voltage divided by secondary voltage, in that order.
For $K>1$, the secondary voltage is lower and the transformer steps voltage down;
for $K<1$, the secondary voltage is higher and it steps voltage up.

